      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pistissophia.2.petermann:129-139",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲙⲏⲓⲧⲛ ⲙⲡⲣϭⲱ **ϩⲓⲃⲟⲗ** ⲙⲙⲟⲛ ·",
      "english": "Come ye inside, remain ye not outside.",
      "source": "The Asceticon of Apa Ephrem part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psephrem.asceticon.budge:24-55",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲉⲩⲛ ⲟⲩϩⲗⲗⲟ ⲇⲉ ⲙⲙⲁⲩ · ⲉϥϣⲁⲛⲣⲟⲉⲓⲥ ⲙⲡⲉϥϩⲟⲟⲩ ϣⲁϥϫⲓϣⲕⲁⲕ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ϫⲉⲃⲱⲕ ⲛⲏⲧⲛ ⲙⲙⲉⲉⲩⲉ ⲉⲧϩⲓϩⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲧϩⲟⲟⲩ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲟⲛ ⲙⲛⲛϩⲁⲗⲁⲁⲧⲉ ⲉⲧ**ϩⲓⲃⲟⲗ** ·",
      "english": "There was an old man there who, when he was guarding on his day, would cry out, 'Go away bad thoughts inside and also birds outside!'",
